The main failure is that the current rules exclude the safe directions (left, and up at (6,1)) because of the `closer_g` sensors, and then fall back to `any`, which lets the adversary pick right. In every listed bad state, right was the losing choice (crash 1.000), and the best choice was left or up. The revised list therefore never chooses right at a crossing unless the other three directions are walls, and it prefers left, then up, then down.

I have not verified this against the exact worst-case computation, so the 0.56 bound is not confirmed. The main risk is that left-first can make Pac loop around the left-hand column (through (3,1) and (3,4)), which ghosts may be able to trap.

```json
{"rules": [
  {"condition": "!wall", "action": "left"},
  {"condition": "!wall", "action": "up"},
  {"condition": "!wall", "action": "down"},
  {"condition": "true", "action": "right"}
]}
```
